{"title":"Staff Nurse Roadmap","role":"Staff Nurse","summary":"A Staff Nurse provides direct patient care in hospitals, clinics, community settings, and other healthcare institutions. The role involves patient assessment, medication administration, monitoring, documentation, infection prevention, patient education, and coordination with doctors and other healthcare professionals.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc Nursing","Course":"Post-Basic B.Sc Nursing"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Staff Nurse provides direct patient care in hospitals, clinics, community settings, and other healthcare institutions. The role involves patient assessment, medication administration, monitoring, documentation, infection prevention, patient education, and coordination with doctors and other healthcare professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"A Post-Basic B.Sc Nursing pathway is designed for candidates who already have a nursing qualification and professional nursing background and want to strengthen their academic and clinical preparation."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest career combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Clinical Nursing","Patient Safety","Medical-Surgical Nursing","Pharmacology","Emergency Care","Documentation","Communication"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Eligibility for Post-Basic B.Sc Nursing generally depends on having the required prior nursing qualification and registration; exact requirements should be checked with the relevant university/nursing authority."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Nursing fundamentals + clinical experience"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Professional Development"},{"text":"Medical-surgical and specialty nursing"}],[{"text":"2030–2032"},{"text":"Post-Basic Study"},{"text":"Advanced nursing knowledge"}],[{"text":"2032–2034"},{"text":"Entry/Transition"},{"text":"Staff Nurse / Clinical Nurse"}],[{"text":"2034–2038"},{"text":"Experienced"},{"text":"Senior Staff Nurse / Specialized Nurse"}],[{"text":"2038–2043"},{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Ward In-Charge / Nursing Supervisor"}],[{"text":"2043+"},{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Nursing Administration / Education"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Strengthen Nursing Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Core Areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Nursing Foundations"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop competence in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vital signs"},{"text":"Patient assessment"},{"text":"Bedside nursing"},{"text":"Personal hygiene"},{"text":"Mobility assistance"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Basic first aid"},{"text":"Nursing documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Teamwork"},{"text":"Clinical discipline"},{"text":"Time management"},{"text":"Nursing ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Medical-Surgical Nursing"},{"type":"p","text":"Medical-surgical nursing should become one of the strongest areas for a Staff Nurse."},{"type":"h","text":"Study"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiovascular disorders"},{"text":"Respiratory disorders"},{"text":"Neurological disorders"},{"text":"Gastrointestinal disorders"},{"text":"Renal diseases"},{"text":"Endocrine disorders"},{"text":"Infectious diseases"},{"text":"Oncology"},{"text":"Orthopedic conditions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Competencies"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Comprehensive patient assessment"},{"text":"Fluid and electrolyte monitoring"}